2.4 Type Modifiers
unsigned int positiveOnly = 4000000000;  // no negative values, larger positive range
signed int normal = -100;                 // default behavior for int

DSA relevance: array indices and sizes are often unsigned internally (size_t) — worth a one-line mention so it's not a mystery later.
2.5 Constants and Literals
const int MAX_SIZE = 100;      // value cannot change after this
#define PI 3.14159             // preprocessor-based constant (older style)

int decimalNum = 100;
int octalNum = 0144;           // prefix 0 = octal
int hexNum = 0x64;             // prefix 0x = hexadecimal
char newline = '\n';           // escape sequence

2.6 Type Conversion / Casting
// Implicit conversion
int a = 5;
double b = a;      // int automatically becomes double: 5.0

// Explicit conversion (casting)
double pi = 3.14;
int truncated = (int)pi;        // C-style cast → 3
int truncated2 = int(pi);        // function-style cast → 3
int truncated3 = static_cast<int>(pi); // modern C++ style → 3

Important gotcha to demonstrate live:
int a = 7, b = 2;
cout << a / b;        // Output: 3 (integer division — decimal truncated!)
cout << (float)a / b; // Output: 3.5 (cast forces decimal division)

